        "original_id": "ed12ff18-980e-5b8e-b46d-1b7409eb4cb6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Béla Bartók, Johann Christoph Pepusch\n- Roles: composer, pianist, ethnomusicologist\n- Works: Rhapsody, Op. 1 (Bartók)\n- Places: Hungary, England\n\nFacts:\n- Béla Bartók was born on 25 March 1881 and died on 26 September 1945.\n- Johann Christoph Pepusch was born in 1667 and died on 20 July 1752.\n- Béla Bartók was a Hungarian composer, pianist, and ethnomusicologist.\n- Johann Christoph Pepusch, also known as John Christopher Pepusch and Dr Pepusch, was a German-born composer.\n- Johann Christoph Pepusch spent most of his working life in England.\n- Rhapsody, Op. 1 is a work by Béla Bartók, identified in the chunk as Sz. 26.",
